---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/Colophon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { getPublishedPosts } from '../lib/writing';

const showWriting = (await getPublishedPosts()).length > 0;
const access = site.links.edgarMiner ?? `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Edgar Miner access')}`;
const accessText = site.links.edgarMiner ? 'Try it.' : 'Ask for access.';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.description}>
  <Nav slot="nav" showWriting={showWriting} />
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>{site.tagline}</h1>
    <p class="purpose">
      I'm Chandni, an engineer who keeps starting companies.
      {site.links.ideas && <a href={site.links.ideas}>Here's the list.</a>}
    </p>

    <p>Right now I'm building <a href="/work/edgar-miner/">Edgar Miner</a> at ThinkMocha. It connects the dots between companies using SEC filings: who supplies whom, who owns what, and where the dependencies are. <a href={access}>{accessText}</a></p>

    {site.hero && <Media items={[site.hero]} />}

    <p>ThinkMocha started somewhere very different.</p>

    <p>One evening, I couldn't convince my then three-year-old to eat her vegetables. So I made her an AI storybook where she was the heroine of a veggie world. She ate the vegetables. I started making books for friends and family, with their children, cultures, and everyday lives in the stories.</p>

    <p>That became <a href="/work/talewriter/">Talewriter</a>. I built it myself and ran a pilot that put 50+ personalized books into a Manhattan preschool. More than 90% of parents and teachers asked for more.</p>

    <p>Before that, I spent six years building backend systems. At Rakuten, I led backend development for <a href="https://www.rakuten.com/dining">Rakuten Dining</a>, a rewards product with 10,000+ restaurants, and helped teams adopt serverless architecture, reducing infrastructure costs by 80%. At <a href="https://www.serverless.com/">Serverless</a>, I rebuilt billing on Stripe and cut processing time by 98%. Earlier, I shipped a Chrome extension that <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2016/08/23/slices-new-browser-add-on-will-email-you-when-prices-drop/">TechCrunch wrote about</a>.</p>

    <p>There have been plenty of other projects along the way.</p>

    <p><a href="/work/fundraising-agent/">Fundraising Agent</a>, which automates investor outreach for founders, bringing the work from 20 hours a week to under two. An events app that never made it beyond my friends. Three hackathon wins involving image recognition, event discovery, and an Arduino scoring system.</p>

    <p>I earned my Tech MBA at NYU Stern in 2026 and screened deep-tech startups for its accelerator. I also apply to YC every year.</p>

    <p class="lines">Some things have worked. Others haven't made it very far. I usually come away with another question I want to build something around.</p>

    <p>I also speak five languages. Happy to start there.</p>

    <p class="ps">P.S. Email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Short emails with a clear ask get answers.</p>
  </section>
  <Colophon slot="colophon" />
</Base>
